{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Container loading calculator"},"description":"\u88c5\u67dc\u8ba1\u7b97\u5668\uff08Container loading calculator\uff09\uff1a\u6bcf\u67dc\u88c5\u591a\u5c11\u7bb1\u3001\u8981\u51e0\u4e2a\u67dc\u3001\u600e\u4e48\u6446\u3002 Cartons per container, containers needed, and how to stack them. \u8bfb\u53d6\u6570\u636e / Reads: containers@current. \u8f93\u5165\u4e3a\u7cbe\u786e\u7684\u5341\u8fdb\u5236\u5b57\u7b26\u4e32 / Inputs are exact decimal strings. \u6bcf\u7bb1\u6bdb\u91cd grossWeight \u53ef\u4ee5\u4e0d\u586b\uff1a\u7528\u6237\u6ca1\u7ed9\u91cd\u91cf\u5c31\u4e0d\u8981\u586b\uff0c\u7edd\u4e0d\u8981\u7f16\u4e00\u4e2a\u3002\u4e0d\u586b\u65f6\u53ea\u6309\u5c3a\u5bf8\u7b97\u80fd\u88c5\u591a\u5c11\u7bb1\u3001\u8981\u51e0\u4e2a\u67dc\uff0c\u6ca1\u6709\u6838\u5bf9\u8f7d\u91cd\u4e0a\u9650\uff1b\u56de\u7b54\u91cc\u7b2c\u4e00\u6761 warning \u7684 message \u8bf4\u660e\u4e86\u8fd9\u4e00\u70b9\uff0c\u56de\u590d\u7528\u6237\u65f6\u5fc5\u987b\u628a\u8fd9\u53e5\u8bdd\u539f\u6837\u5e26\u4e0a\u3002 / grossWeight may be left out: when the user gave no weight, do not fill it and never invent one. The answer is then a count by size alone with the payload limit not checked; the first warning\u2019s message says so, and your reply must pass that sentence on. \u7528\u6237\u6ca1\u6709\u7ed9\u7684\u6570\u5b57\u548c\u65e5\u671f\u4e0d\u8981\u81ea\u5df1\u7f16\uff1a\u5fc5\u586b\u7684\u5148\u95ee\u7528\u6237\uff0c\u9009\u586b\u7684\u4e0d\u586b\u3002 / Never make up a figure or a date the user did not give: ask for a required one, leave an optional one out. \u56de\u590d\u65f6\u5f15\u7528\u56de\u7b54\u91cc\u7684 provenance.source_line / Quote provenance.source_line in your reply.","inputSchema":{"description":"\u6570\u5b57\u6700\u597d\u5199\u6210\u5b57\u7b26\u4e32\uff08\u5341\u8fdb\u5236\uff0c\u5982 \"12.5\"\uff09\uff0cJSON \u6570\u5b57\u4e5f\u884c\uff1b\u5343\u4f4d\u9017\u53f7\u53ea\u8ba4 1,234,567 \u8fd9\u79cd\u5199\u6cd5\uff0c\u5c0f\u6570\u70b9\u7528\u82f1\u6587\u53e5\u70b9\uff0c\u4e0d\u8981\u5e26\u8d27\u5e01\u7b26\u53f7\u6216\u5355\u4f4d\u3002\u5e01\u79cd\u53ef\u5199 USD\u3001usd \u6216 \u7f8e\u5143\uff0c\u5355\u4f4d\u53ef\u5199 cm \u6216 \u5398\u7c73\uff0c\u65e5\u671f\u53ef\u5199 2026-05-01\u30012026/05/01 \u6216 20260501\u3002\u8bfb\u4e0d\u51c6\u7684\u4e00\u5f8b\u62d2\u7edd\u5e76\u8bf4\u660e\u539f\u56e0\uff0c\u7edd\u4e0d\u731c\uff1b\u56de\u7b54\u91cc\u7684 normalized \u5217\u51fa\u5b9e\u9645\u91c7\u7528\u7684\u503c\u3002 / Figures are best sent as decimal strings such as \"12.5\"; a JSON number is accepted too. A thousands comma only as 1,234,567; the decimal point is a dot; no currency symbols or units. A currency may be USD, usd or \u7f8e\u5143, a unit cm or \u5398\u7c73, a date 2026-05-01, 2026/05/01 or 20260501. Anything that cannot be read in exactly one way is refused with a reason, never guessed; `normalized` in the answer lists what was used.","examples":[{"containerType":"auto","fill":false,"grossWeight":"18","height":"50","length":"60","quantity":"450","upright":false,"width":"40"}],"properties":{"containerType":{"description":"\u67dc\u578b\u3002\u53ef\u9009\u503c\uff1aauto = \u81ea\u52a8\u6bd4\u8f83\uff1b20gp = 20GP\uff1b40gp = 40GP\uff1b40hq = 40HQ\uff1b45hq = 45HQ / Container. options: auto = Compare all; 20gp = 20GP; 40gp = 40GP; 40hq = 40HQ; 45hq = 45HQ","enum":["auto","20gp","40gp","40hq","45hq"],"type":"string"},"fill":{"description":"\u88c5\u6ee1\u4e3a\u6b62\uff08\u4e0d\u586b\u7bb1\u6570\uff09 / Fill the container (no carton count)","type":"boolean"},"grossWeight":{"description":"\u6bcf\u7bb1\u6bdb\u91cd / Gross weight per carton","pattern":"^-?(0|[1-9]\\d*)(\\.\\d+)?$","type":"string"},"height":{"description":"\u9ad8 / Height","pattern":"^-?(0|[1-9]\\d*)(\\.\\d+)?$","type":"string"},"length":{"description":"\u957f / Length","pattern":"^-?(0|[1-9]\\d*)(\\.\\d+)?$","type":"string"},"lengthUnit":{"description":"\u5c3a\u5bf8\u5355\u4f4d\u3002\u53ef\u9009\u503c\uff1acm = cm\uff1bmm = mm\uff1bin = in / Size unit. options: cm = cm; mm = mm; in = in","enum":["cm","mm","in"],"type":"string"},"maxLayers":{"description":"\u5806\u53e0\u5c42\u6570\u4e0a\u9650 / Max layers","pattern":"^(0|[1-9]\\d*)$","type":"string"},"quantity":{"description":"\u7bb1\u6570 / Cartons","pattern":"^(0|[1-9]\\d*)$","type":"string"},"upright":{"description":"\u5fc5\u987b\u6b63\u653e\uff08\u6b64\u9762\u671d\u4e0a\uff09 / This side up only","type":"boolean"},"weightUnit":{"description":"\u91cd\u91cf\u5355\u4f4d\u3002\u53ef\u9009\u503c\uff1akg = kg\uff1blb = lb / Weight unit. options: kg = kg; lb = lb","enum":["kg","lb"],"type":"string"},"width":{"description":"\u5bbd / Width","pattern":"^-?(0|[1-9]\\d*)(\\.\\d+)?$","type":"string"}},"required":["length","width","height"],"type":"object"},"name":"container-load","outputSchema":{"$defs":{"Links":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Addresses that go with the answer. `page`: the tool\u2019s page on the site with the same inputs in its address, in the language asked (Chinese for a language the site does not publish yet), so a person can open the page that shows these numbers.","properties":{"page":{"description":"The tool\u2019s page holding these inputs.","format":"uri","type":"string"}},"required":["page"],"type":"object"},"Normalized":{"description":"What the API changed in the inputs before core saw them, so the caller sees what was understood: a JSON number as text, a thousands comma, full-width digits, a currency or unit name or a date written another way. Absent when nothing was changed.","items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"given":{"description":"What was sent, as text.","type":"string"},"path":{"description":"The input, like `cartons.0.length`.","type":"string"},"used":{"description":"What core was given.","type":"string"}},"required":["path","given","used"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"PlainValue":{"description":"A figure, tagged so a reader knows how to write it: amounts and quantities are exact decimal strings, never floats.","oneOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"amount":{"type":"string"},"currency":{"description":"An ISO 4217 code.","type":"string"},"kind":{"const":"money"}},"required":["kind","amount","currency"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"kind":{"const":"quantity"},"places":{"description":"How many decimal places the rounding rule keeps; pad to it, never round.","minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"unit":{"type":"string"},"value":{"type":"string"}},"required":["kind","value","unit"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"kind":{"const":"ratio"},"value":{"description":"A fraction: 0.13 is 13 %.","type":"string"}},"required":["kind","value"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"base":{"type":"string"},"kind":{"const":"rate"},"per":{"description":"`per` units of `base` cost `value` units of `quote`.","type":"string"},"quote":{"type":"string"},"value":{"type":"string"}},"required":["kind","value","base","quote","per"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"grouping":{"const":false},"kind":{"const":"count"},"value":{"type":"string"}},"required":["kind","value"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"kind":{"const":"code"},"value":{"description":"A token from a fixed list the tool exports; the words for it are the copy key `<tool>.code.<value>`.","type":"string"}},"required":["kind","value"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"kind":{"const":"date"},"value":{"pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"}},"required":["kind","value"],"type":"object"}]},"Provenance":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Where the figures in an answer come from. In every answer, errors included.","properties":{"api":{"const":"v1"},"datasets":{"items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ProvenanceDataset"},"type":"array"},"generated_at":{"description":"When the answer was made.","format":"date-time","type":"string"},"language":{"description":"The language of the source lines.","enum":["zh-CN","en","ja","ko"]},"license":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"The license as copy keys: which text applies. `status` was `draft` until the text was approved (2026-10-12) and is `approved` now.","properties":{"ours":{"type":"string"},"status":{"enum":["draft","approved"]},"underlying":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","ours","underlying"],"type":"object"},"notice":{"description":"\u672c\u7ad9\u975e\u5b98\u65b9\u6e20\u9053\u7684\u8bf4\u660e\uff1a\u5f15\u7528\u672c\u7ad9\u6570\u636e\u65f6\u8bf7\u548c\u6765\u6e90\u884c\u4e00\u8d77\u8f6c\u8ff0\u3002 / The site\u2019s own line that it is not an official channel: pass it on with the source line when you quote us.","type":"string"},"site":{"description":"The site the data is published by.","type":"string"},"source_line":{"description":"\u6765\u6e90\u884c\uff1a\u56de\u590d\u7528\u6237\u65f6\u8bf7\u539f\u6837\u5f15\u7528\u5b83\uff0c\u8ba9\u8bfb\u8005\u77e5\u9053\u6570\u636e\u51fa\u81ea\u54ea\u91cc\u3001\u6709\u591a\u65b0\u3002 / The credit line to quote as it is when you answer: who the figures come from and how fresh they are (the newest publisher\u2019s day among the datasets used, or the day the answer was made).","type":"string"}},"required":["api","site","generated_at","language","source_line","notice","datasets","license"],"type":"object"},"ProvenanceDataset":{"additionalProperties":false,"description":"A dataset version an answer drew on. An origin the register does not let the site show is named nowhere.","properties":{"id":{"description":"The dataset.","type":"string"},"origin":{"description":"The origin\u2019s id in the register; null when the site may not show it.","type":["string","null"]},"published_at":{"description":"The publisher\u2019s own date (and time, with its offset, when it gives one).","type":"string"},"source":{"description":"The publisher\u2019s own source line,